.SH NAME
parking\-report\-http \- authenticated, login\-only HTTP adapter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B parking\-report\-http
[\fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Authenticated, login\-only HTTP adapter. Report submission is not
enabled.
.PP
Serves the login\-only adapter on 0.0.0.0:PORT until stopped. Other
command\-line arguments are ignored. An invalid configuration exits 1
with a fixed message and no exception text. See docs/HTTP106.md.
.PP
JSON output: HTTP responses only; see docs/HTTP106.md.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show this help message and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBPARKING_HTTP_TOKEN\fR
Private bearer token, at least 32 characters (required)
.TP
\fBPORT\fR
TCP port to listen on, 1\-65535 (default 10000)
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
\-h/\-\-help: help text on stdout, before configuration is read or a
socket is bound.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid configuration: fixed message on stderr, no exception text.
